From 0ef3eae4ad70cd67642e2943f3f249e507d6b750 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 19:23:36 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] quiet-hold: preflight the gateway's host-file start
 refusals before the lease commits the 2 h cooldown

Five whys (live, worker-2, 11:04 PST 2026-11-13, gateway on dd75da236bca):
1. Why did worker-2 lose its quiet proof slot for 2 h? `hermes kanban quiet-hold` took the
   claim-quiet lease, which commits `last-started.json` (the 2 h cooldown), and only then did the
   gateway's `quiet-observe-start` refuse with `update_window_stale` 0.46 s later.
2. Why was the start doomed? `QuietControl.start()` refuses unless `cache/core-update/window.json`
   is this host's, `idle`, and at most UPDATE_WINDOW_MAX_AGE_S = 120 s old; worker-2's record was
   295 s old (workers republish it from the 10-minute hermes-core-update.timer), and Macs/hub are
   often `batching`/`draining`.
3. Why wasn't that seen first? `hold()` called `claim_quiet.acquire()` before reading anything,
   although those refusals come from host files readable without a lease.

Fix:
- gateway/quiet_control.py: split the file-backed part of `_update_status` (drain/admission hold,
  deploy window) into `_hold_reasons()` / `_window_status(now)`, and add
  `start_preflight_reasons(now=None, margin_s=START_PREFLIGHT_MARGIN_S=30)`: the same readers and
  reason spellings as `start()` (`update:<reason>`, then `update_window_stale`), with the freshness
  bound tightened by 30 s so a window that goes stale during the observer's spawn/handshake is
  refused up front. `start()` itself is unchanged in behaviour.
- hermes_cli/kanban_quiet.py: `hold()` runs that preflight before `acquire`; any reason (or an
  unreadable preflight) exits 78 (EXIT_PREFLIGHT) with no lease, no cooldown, no observer. Once a
  start is attempted, lease and cooldown semantics are unchanged.
- Runner-only refusals (attestation route, coverage pending, registry unknowns, drain/restart
  flags) are exposed by no read-only control verb, so they remain the gateway's own refusal after
  the lease; documented in the module docstring.
- Pool workers: documented as not quiet-proof targets (the live quiet proof is owned on the Macs).
  Their 10-minute window republish and batching make the 120 s bound usually unmet; the preflight
  now turns a worker attempt into a free exit 78 instead of a burned cooldown, so no publisher
  cadence or max-age change.

Tests:
- tests/hermes_cli/test_kanban_quiet.py: stale (295 s, worker-2's live age), batching and draining
  windows exit 78 through the real CLI without writing last-started.json or starting the observer,
  and an immediate retry with an idle window succeeds; missing window / inside-the-margin window
  and an exploding preflight refuse. The `home` fixture now writes a fresh idle window.
- tests/gateway/test_quiet_control.py: preflight(margin 0) equals start()'s refusal reasons for
  draining/batching/stale/missing/idle windows; the margin refuses a 115 s-old window.
RED on the parent (tests only): 11 failed, incl. "cooldown was committed" for all three windows.
GREEN: test_kanban_quiet 19/19, test_quiet_control 57/57, test_observe_gateway_quiet 48/48,
test_quiet_membership_seeding 8/8, test_code_attestation_deps.
---
